<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:17:04 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen: Why the Houthis may besiege Aden rather than storm it</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-yemen-why-the-houthis-may-besiege-aden-rather-than-storm-it</link><description>
Bolstered by their recent military successes, Houthi rebels this week advanced close to the southern port city of Aden, the interim capital of the internationally recognised Yemeni government. Amid territorial ambitions, regional rivalries, and divisions within government forces, the potential fall of this stronghold could permanently alter the balance of power in the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a907106-e35a-11f1-a33f-dbb3dc175088</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:55:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg">© Abdulnasser Alseddik, AP</source><dc:creator>Marc DAOU</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: Israel launches ground operation in Hamas-held area of Gaza</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-middle-east-live-kuwait-bahrain-report-drone-and-missile-attacks</link><description>
The Israeli military said Wednesday its forces were targeting Hamas infrastructure outside areas it controls in the Gaza Strip as a local journalist reported seeing Israeli tanks positioned east of the Nuseirat refugee camp. Earlier, Iran warned that it would retaliate in a "more devastating" manner if the United States and its allies launched new attacks on its territory. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c27f5ac4-e368-11f1-97ec-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321586490001.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c27f5ac4-e368-11f1-97ec-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321586490001.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1668ed4-e2f4-11f1-bc21-b5a4f32090d0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:06:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c27f5ac4-e368-11f1-97ec-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321586490001.jpg">© Jehad Alshrafi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli parliament elects Eisenkot ally Matan Kahana as speaker in blow for Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261117-%F0%9F%94%B4-israeli-parliament-elects-eisenkot-ally-matan-kahana-as-speaker</link><description>
The Israeli parliament on Tuesday elected as new speaker an ally of Gadi Eisenkot, the party leader currently working to form the next government and replace current Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Matan Kahana, a former special forces soldier, is expected as soon as Wednesday to start the process of undoing much of the agenda of Netanyahu.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/855e62f8-e290-11f1-bec3-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321467242182.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/855e62f8-e290-11f1-bec3-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321467242182.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06a31598-e2cd-11f1-95a7-ef5f71c47c23</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:24:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/855e62f8-e290-11f1-bec3-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321467242182.jpg">© Ohad Zwigenberg, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Major setbacks for Netanyahu ahead of vote to name new Knesset speaker</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/major-setbacks-for-netanyahu-ahead-of-vote-to-name-new-knesset-speaker</link><description>
Since suffering heavy losses in Israel’s Oct. 27 election, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's party has repeatedly claimed the vote was “stolen” by Arab-led parties, possibly with foreign assistance. Those claims appear to be crumbling as he tries to cling to power, as the Israeli parliament is set to select a new speaker opposed to him. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e0651c4-e2c8-11f1-a84f-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-213508-213905-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e0651c4-e2c8-11f1-a84f-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-213508-213905-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63d70684-e2c8-11f1-9b2a-e9eb4a134bed</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:05:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Did the US use ‘blackout bombs’ in Iran? Images reveal mysterious fibres at infrastructure sites</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261117-iran-us-graphite-blackout-bombs-infrastructure</link><description>
Photographs published by Iranian local media suggest that US forces may have used graphite bombs, also known as ‘blackout bombs’, against infrastructure in Iran in recent days. These weapons are designed to disrupt electricity supplies by causing short circuits rather than physically destroying power facilities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ac6122-e286-11f1-9631-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-2026-11-17-13-57-17.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ac6122-e286-11f1-9631-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-2026-11-17-13-57-17.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">abbdb91a-e288-11f1-9ecb-bbc38acb6f61</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:39:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ac6122-e286-11f1-9631-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-2026-11-17-13-57-17.jpg">© Iran Didehban</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Breaking taboos: Egypt's sexual revolution takes to social media</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261116-breaking-taboos-egypt-s-sexual-revolution-takes-to-social-media</link><description>
In Egypt, a sexual revolution is quietly unfolding on social media. Accounts followed by tens of thousands of people, with posts attracting millions of views, are tackling a wide range of issues surrounding sexuality – from the widespread practice of female genital mutilation (which 93 per cent of women in rural areas have undergone) to sex education and sexual pleasure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1e52f70-df7e-11f1-ba40-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-F24-FOCUS-EGYPT-SEXUALITY-NO-MIX-Video-Mixdown-4-FF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1e52f70-df7e-11f1-ba40-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-F24-FOCUS-EGYPT-SEXUALITY-NO-MIX-Video-Mixdown-4-FF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f0ea93a-df7f-11f1-8f29-756da825505b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:50:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Mathilde DELVIGNE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Eisenkot says Netanyahu ‘cannot remain’ after alleged election interference by aide</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261116-eisenkot-netanyahu-cannot-stay-in-office</link><description>
Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot said on Sunday caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu must leave office immediately following reports of alleged electoral interference by a Netanyahu aide. The former army chief called Netanyahu and his entourage an "immediate threat to democracy", hours after representatives discussed forming a national unity government.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">615a1e8c-e16f-11f1-b66f-d18c20ac47cd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:47:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg">© Ohad Zwigenberg, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Houthis advance on Aden as government forces retreat to defend their capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-yemen-houthis-advance-to-within-60-kilometres-of-aden-military-sources-say</link><description>
Houthi forces in Yemen have advanced to within 60 kilometres of Aden, the seat of the country's internationally recognised government, military and government sources said Sunday. The embattled government earlier announced it was pulling back its last forces from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait to defend its temporary capital on the southern coast of Yemen. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92e0513c-e12a-11f1-8ab7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T135302Z-1473180222-RC26OOADAAUR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-DETAINEES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92e0513c-e12a-11f1-8ab7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T135302Z-1473180222-RC26OOADAAUR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-DETAINEES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f89ab374-e129-11f1-810f-b5965fbe9753</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:28:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92e0513c-e12a-11f1-8ab7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T135302Z-1473180222-RC26OOADAAUR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-DETAINEES.jpg">© Khaled Abdullah, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel kills senior member of Hamas's military wing in Gaza strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-israel-kills-senior-member-of-hamas-s-military-wing-in-gaza-strike</link><description>
The Israeli military said on Sunday its forces had killed a senior member of Hamas's military wing in Gaza. The militant group confirmed the death of Samir Abu Younis, the commander of its Rafah brigade, adding that he played a prominent role in planning the October 7, 2023 attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8bd9500-e110-11f1-96bd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T084533Z-1916440832-RC27OOA15A2T-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-HAMAS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8bd9500-e110-11f1-96bd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T084533Z-1916440832-RC27OOA15A2T-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-HAMAS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5d92877e-e112-11f1-80af-bf3cc1bef008</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:41:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8bd9500-e110-11f1-96bd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T084533Z-1916440832-RC27OOA15A2T-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-HAMAS.jpg">© Haseeb Alwazeer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran claims drone attack on US military base in Bahrain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-claims-drone-attack-on-us-military-base-in-bahrain</link><description>
Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September as blasts rocked the capital, Manama. It comes after Iran targeted an airbase in the US-allied island state, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East War and comes as negotiations to end the conflict remain at a stalemate, with the US maintaining its naval blockade and Iran its stranglehold over the strait of Hormuz. Story by Rachael Griffiths.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc1d38c8-e108-11f1-8b7b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160212-160405-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc1d38c8-e108-11f1-8b7b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160212-160405-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e170475c-e108-11f1-ab96-f165ee9aaa0a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:29:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bahrain says air defences destroyed several Iranian drones attacking US base</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bahrain-says-air-defences-destroyed-several-iranian-drones-attacking-us-base</link><description>
Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September. The second Iranian drone attack in three days, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East war. Diplomatic efforts to end the almost nine-month conflict have yet to produce a breakthrough, with ​sporadic attacks continuing. Details from the ground by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Tehran, Reza Sayah.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84b2607c-e0f9-11f1-b274-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-130317-130744-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84b2607c-e0f9-11f1-b274-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-130317-130744-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89cee620-e0f9-11f1-b619-d9dce5f4b66f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:55:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Global diesel prices ease as winter approaches</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/global-diesel-prices-ease-as-winter-approaches</link><description>
Global diesel prices, which have remained elevated since the start of the Iran war and the blockade of the Strait of Hormuz, have fallen sharply in recent weeks as Gulf exports recover and global oil supplies get back on track for the first time since February. The price drop is being felt in Europe, where prices remain roughly 77% above pre-war levels, and in the US, where the national average fell below $6 a gallon on Saturday. Details by Liza Kaminov.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2255b7f8-e0e0-11f1-a02e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-100412-100553-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2255b7f8-e0e0-11f1-a02e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-100412-100553-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">281836fc-e0e0-11f1-ad3e-9f4696c62486</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:40:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran claims drone attack on US military airbase in Bahrain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-iran-claims-attack-on-us-military-airbase-in-bahrain</link><description>
Iranian military confirmed on Sunday an attack on a US military base in Bahrain, in its second targeting the Middle Eastern country in the space of three days. Bahrain's military said it had intercepted several Iranian attacks, with the foreign ministry confirming its air defence systems had shot down Iranian drones, preventing them from reaching their intended targets.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3bb0cb5a-e0d8-11f1-a866-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/000-99GY7E6-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3bb0cb5a-e0d8-11f1-a866-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/000-99GY7E6-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a80550d4-e0d6-11f1-997f-8119674c1597</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:57:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3bb0cb5a-e0d8-11f1-a866-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/000-99GY7E6-1.jpg">© 2026 Planet Labs PBC, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Three sentenced to death over Jordan church attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-three-sentenced-to-death-over-jordan-church-attack</link><description>
A Jordanian court on Sunday sentenced the three gunmen responsible for a terror attack on a church funeral procession in the village of Hamoud that killed nine and wounded others. The attack prompted retaliatory strikes on "terrorist organisations" in neighbouring Syria. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb10e528-e0d1-11f1-ba89-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299487770405.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb10e528-e0d1-11f1-ba89-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299487770405.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41467eaa-e0d0-11f1-ab7a-d9b8b6b92b26</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:53:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb10e528-e0d1-11f1-ba89-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299487770405.jpg">© Raad Adayleh, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu renews call for Israeli unity government as Eisenkot dismisses 'tricks'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261114-netanyahu-renews-call-for-israeli-government-unity-as-eisenkot-dismisses-tricks</link><description>
Israeli caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Saturday renewed his call for a national unity government with Gadi Eisenkot, who dismissed the appeal as a political ploy. This comes as the incoming premier is in the midst of negotiations to form a new administration.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9d87c1e-e06a-11f1-b45a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/eb428c66bf6978a929203d6ac1afd3964fb560b1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9d87c1e-e06a-11f1-b45a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/eb428c66bf6978a929203d6ac1afd3964fb560b1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eac268f6-e06a-11f1-afd8-addf77e06d09</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:35:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9d87c1e-e06a-11f1-b45a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/eb428c66bf6978a929203d6ac1afd3964fb560b1.jpg">© Ilia Yefimovich, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Turkey and Qatar pledge unified stance against attacks in mutual defence pact</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261113-turkey-and-qatar-pledge-unified-stance-against-attacks-in-mutual-defence-pact</link><description>
Turkey and Qatar signed a mutual defence agreement Friday, pledging a unified response to any attack on either country, the two leaders said in a joint statement. The defence pact follows the Mecca Joint Defence Agreement signed by Turkey, Pakistan and Saudi Arabia in August.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e18af32-df9b-11f1-903b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T145055Z-1247391648-RC22NOA8HWLE-RTRMADP-3-TURKEY-QATAR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e18af32-df9b-11f1-903b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T145055Z-1247391648-RC22NOA8HWLE-RTRMADP-3-TURKEY-QATAR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2bd949e-df99-11f1-bdcc-23840e8dab80</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:06:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e18af32-df9b-11f1-903b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T145055Z-1247391648-RC22NOA8HWLE-RTRMADP-3-TURKEY-QATAR.jpg">© Murat Cetinmuhurdar, Turkish Presidential Press Office via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>West Bank: ‘Without international trade and financial support, large settlements would not exist’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exist-1</link><description>
France is considering legislation to restrict trade with Israeli settlements in the occupied Palestinian territories, namely the West Bank. Ivar Ekeland, Professor Emeritus at Paris Dauphine-PSL University and Chair of the Organization of Academics for the Respect of International Law in Palestine, discusses the proposed measures with Alison Sargent. He calls for restrictions to cover n ot only goods but also services, including financial services, insurance and tourism. "Without the support of financial entities, of insurance, of providing goods and so on, settlements, big settlements, would not exist," he argues.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d3f7e80-df7b-11f1-aba2-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-080847-081941-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d3f7e80-df7b-11f1-aba2-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-080847-081941-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8270b5ae-df7b-11f1-9261-bb9885e86514</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:15:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>UN refugee chief Barham Salih slams 'shameful' war in Sudan, urges 'political solution'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261113-un-refugee-chief-barham-salih-slams-shameful-war-in-sudan-urges-political-solution</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, UN refugee chief Barham Salih called the war in Sudan "shameful" and urged the world to end it. With forced displacement at a record high, he warned that funding cuts are hurting people "in dire need". "Efficiency has its limits," he said. Salih also defended the "integrity of the asylum system".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02c9f834-dea3-11f1-84f2-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/TaT-BARHAM-SALIH-pour-mix-V2-MIX-OK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02c9f834-dea3-11f1-84f2-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/TaT-BARHAM-SALIH-pour-mix-V2-MIX-OK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">37a844bc-dea7-11f1-8b75-1591d7fd5df4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:56:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>The truth about Douma: How Syria covered up a chemical attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261113-the-truth-about-douma-how-syria-covered-up-a-chemical-attack</link><description>
On April 7, 2018, the Syrian town of Douma, on the outskirts of the capital Damascus, was targeted by a chemical attack. Evidence pointed to the Syrian regime, yet proof vanished, and eyewitnesses went silent. Eight years later, FRANCE 24's Jenna Le Bras tracked down survivors and witnesses of the deadly attack. She also met representatives of some of the world's most powerful institutions to understand how a massive cover-up campaign had been orchestrated by the regime, with Russian support.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6393738e-df57-11f1-9809-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-douma-mensonge-d-etat-EN-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6393738e-df57-11f1-9809-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-douma-mensonge-d-etat-EN-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">94e4bbda-df68-11f1-bace-abe937de67c9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:24:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jenna LE BRAS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>'No war, no peace' situation between US and Iran 'cannot continue', Iraqi FM says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261113-no-war-and-no-peace-between-the-us-and-iran-cannot-continue-iraqi-fm-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Iraqi Foreign Minister Fuad Hussein said the "no war and no peace" situation in the region "cannot continue". He also said that closing all but two border crossings with Iran, as Washington demands, was "not possible". Finally, he confirmed that Iraqi oil now is now flowing through the Strait of Hormuz under US protection.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36d19004-de87-11f1-be18-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/TETE-A-TETE-HUSSEIN-FOUAD-MIX-OK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36d19004-de87-11f1-be18-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/TETE-A-TETE-HUSSEIN-FOUAD-MIX-OK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddff67ee-de81-11f1-a151-6b48e96878ad</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:28:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli strike on Gaza hospital kills six, including surgeon, medics say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-strike-on-gaza-hospital-kills-six-including-surgeon-medics-say</link><description>
Israeli fire killed 11 people in Gaza on Thursday, six of them in the bombing of Nasser hospital in south Gaza early in the day, health officials said, the deadliest single strike since Israel's elections last month. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Dr Goher Rahbour, a surgeon working at the Nasser Hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8bb4c84-ded2-11f1-b9be-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-203639-204648-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8bb4c84-ded2-11f1-b9be-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-203639-204648-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddeb127a-ded2-11f1-aba1-f38243617a56</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:03:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel to ban far-left French politician Jean-Luc Mélenchon from entry</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-to-ban-far-left-french-politician-jean-luc-m%C3%A9lenchon-from-entry</link><description>
The Israeli government said Thursday that it would ban far-left French leader Jean-Luc Mélenchon from entering the country after the French presidential contender said he would use French vessels to force aid into Gaza if he were elected. The announcement comes a day after France confirmed it had refused entry to the head of a body representing settlements in the occupied West Bank.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33654616-dab0-11f1-ad25-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T100614Z-1152484815-RC2Y2OATJ5N2-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33654616-dab0-11f1-ad25-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T100614Z-1152484815-RC2Y2OATJ5N2-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8866be1e-debc-11f1-bc46-a78d57209718</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:43:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33654616-dab0-11f1-ad25-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T100614Z-1152484815-RC2Y2OATJ5N2-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg">© Abdul Saboor, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel kills six in Gaza hospital strike as 9-month-old baby freezes to death</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-kills-six-in-gaza-hospital-strike-as-9-month-old-baby-freezes-to-death</link><description>
An overnight Israeli air strike on Nasser Hospital in southern Gaza killed at least six Palestinians Thursday, including a teenage boy and a surgeon, medics said. Elsewhere in the devastated Palestinian territory, a nine-month-old baby died from the cold as families flee worsening flooding.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2915f31c-dead-11f1-ba4a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T043325Z-1772503551-RC23MOA2UKYO-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2915f31c-dead-11f1-ba4a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T043325Z-1772503551-RC23MOA2UKYO-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb02b8d8-deac-11f1-8b1d-e74430e79b3b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:18:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2915f31c-dead-11f1-ba4a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T043325Z-1772503551-RC23MOA2UKYO-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg">© Ramadan Abed, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>How FRANCE 24 traced Tehran-backed Afghan fighters from Syria to southeastern Iran</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-iran-afghan-fatemiyoun-fighters-syria-baluchistan</link><description>
Members of the Tehran-backed Afghan Shia militia known as the Fatemiyoun division have resurfaced in Iran after largely disappearing from public view following the fall of Bashar al-Assad’s government in Syria in 2024. FRANCE 24 used "martyrdom” announcements and the geolocation of videos shared on social media to trace their presence. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84498144-dea4-11f1-ad4b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/fat-main-photo.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84498144-dea4-11f1-ad4b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/fat-main-photo.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d6127e6-dea7-11f1-884f-3be5653ca07f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:03:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84498144-dea4-11f1-ad4b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/fat-main-photo.jpg">© Observers</source><dc:creator>Ershad ALIJANI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Israeli occupation in southern Lebanon: Displaced families struggle to cope</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261112-israeli-occupation-in-southern-lebanon-displaced-families-struggle-to-cope</link><description>
In Lebanon, more than 360,000 people are still displaced after months of war between Israel and Hezbollah, according to the UN. Along the border, the Israeli army claims to be fighting the Iran-backed militant group but now occupies 6 percent of Lebanese territory and is wiping entire villages off the map. In the border area, we meet families living in makeshift housing. Many fear they may never go home.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38e48628-ddf9-11f1-82b6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-FREEZE-LEBANON-ISRAELI-OCCUPATION-BAIN-Lauren-Sub.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38e48628-ddf9-11f1-82b6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-FREEZE-LEBANON-ISRAELI-OCCUPATION-BAIN-Lauren-Sub.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7e34142-ddf9-11f1-ba1f-d72171b1cb65</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:51:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sophie GUIGNON</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Gadi Eisenkot unveils agenda to reverse Netanyahu’s policies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261111-gadi-eisenkot-unveils-agenda-to-reverse-netanyahu-s-policies</link><description>
The bloc of Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot introduced a series of bills at the start of the legislative session that target Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his policies. They include launching an official government-led inquiry into the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks, setting term limits on the position of prime minister and overturning changes the outgoing Netanyahu-led government made to limit the powers of the judiciary. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Rina Bassist, Editor at Al-Monitor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b2b3982-de7a-11f1-9d73-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f44ef0f1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b2b3982-de7a-11f1-9d73-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f44ef0f1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">122ae710-de1d-11f1-aaa4-c1c2bf00e785</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:13:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gadi Eisenkot unveils agenda to reverse Netanyahu’s policies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-unveils-agenda-to-reverse-netanyahu-s-policies</link><description>
The bloc of Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot introduced a series of bills at the start of the legislative session that target Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his policies. They include launching an official government-led inquiry into the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks, setting term limits on the position of prime minister and overturning changes the outgoing Netanyahu-led government made to limit the powers of the judiciary. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Rina Bassist, Editor at Al-Monitor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b2b3982-de7a-11f1-9d73-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f44ef0f1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b2b3982-de7a-11f1-9d73-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f44ef0f1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf1f26bc-de1b-11f1-828e-f1fb8133ff5f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:11:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Eisenkot quickly targets Netanyahu's legacy in new Israeli parliament</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eisenkot-quickly-targets-netanyahu-s-legacy-in-new-israeli-parliament</link><description>
Israeli ex-army chief Gadi Eisenkot and his allies launched a legislative onslaught against caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's legacy on Tuesday, as a new parliament convened in a heated first session.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8491a9b4-ddb0-11f1-897d-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-080849-081212-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8491a9b4-ddb0-11f1-897d-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-080849-081212-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">895e049c-ddb0-11f1-a157-7b99786cc99c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:29:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Egyptian journalist Lina Attalah faces prison as trial sparks international outcry</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261111-lina-attalah-egypt-trial-prison</link><description>
Egyptian journalist Lina Attalah, head of independent news outlet Mada Masr, faces a criminal court retrial Wednesday over charges of operating without a licence and publishing false news. The UN criticised Egypt’s “widening assaults on press freedom” Tuesday. Attalah was previously handed a one-year prison sentence in absentia in 2024.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f471bf6c-dd6f-11f1-b88a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/a44f4102d9b1178ba8efb41cfeca20fa077097ab.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f471bf6c-dd6f-11f1-b88a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/a44f4102d9b1178ba8efb41cfeca20fa077097ab.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b28f2c5e-dd71-11f1-9beb-d78b5b97da2a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:53:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f471bf6c-dd6f-11f1-b88a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/a44f4102d9b1178ba8efb41cfeca20fa077097ab.jpg">© Khaled Desouki, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Eisenkot pushes October 7 inquiry as Netanyahu targets Arab parties in tense new parliament</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-eisenkot-pushes-october-7-inquiry-as-netanyahu-targets-arab-parties-in-tense-new-parliament</link><description>
Gadi Eisenkot, the politician tasked with forming a new Israeli government, pledged on Tuesday to launch an official inquiry into Hamas's October 7, 2023 attacks and reverse many of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's policies as the new parliament was sworn in a tense opening session that saw rival parties trade barbs over the possibility of forming a government with the support of Arab lists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4b03f38-dd4f-11f1-8261-3ba878fe5186</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:53:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg">© Ohad Zwigenberg, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
